IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc12-order-67`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore) -- tests for Order 67 (roc12-order-67.l4).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the Rule (lines 7569 to 7661 of the source file) before the run.
-- The dates are made up; the last day of each 14-day period is an input from Order 3, Rule 3 (here 24 March 2025).

§ `O 67 r 1`
#ASSERT `o 67 r 1(1) the enactment is the Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- ""Act" means the Terrorism (Suppression of Financing) Act"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 1(1) the enactment is the Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "means"
-- r 1(2).  Arguments: the expression is used in the Act; whether it has that meaning in the Act (an input; the Act is not among the sources).
#ASSERT `o 67 r 1(2) the expression has in this Order the meaning it has in the Act` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the Act's answer is passed through
#ASSERT `o 67 r 1(2) the expression has in this Order the meaning it has in the Act` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- likewise
#ASSERT `o 67 r 1(2) the expression has in this Order the meaning it has in the Act` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- the Act is not among the sources
#ASSERT `o 67 r 1(2) the expression has in this Order the meaning it has in the Act` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING -- "Expressions used in this Order which are used in the Act": an expression not in the Act is outside
-- r 1(3).  Arguments: an action is pending; made by summons in the action; made by originating application.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 1(3) the application is made in the way the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a): pending, by summons in the action
#ASSERT `o 67 r 1(3) the application is made in the way the Rule requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: pending but made by originating application
#ASSERT `o 67 r 1(3) the application is made in the way the Rule requires` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b): no action pending, by originating application
#ASSERT `o 67 r 1(3) the application is made in the way the Rule requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: no action pending but made by summons
-- r 1(4).
#ASSERT `o 67 r 1(4) this Order applies in the court` `State Courts` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "This Order is not applicable to the State Courts"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 1(4) this Order applies in the court` `Supreme Court` EQUALS NOTHING -- the paragraph says nothing of the Supreme Court

§ `O 67 r 2`
-- r 2(1).  Arguments: the kind of application; made without notice.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(1) the application is made as the Rule requires` `o 67 r 2(1)(a) an application for a warrant for search and seizure under section 11(1)(a)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a) without notice
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(1) the application is made as the Rule requires` `o 67 r 2(1)(a) an application for a warrant for search and seizure under section 11(1)(a)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: (a) with notice
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(1) the application is made as the Rule requires` `o 67 r 2(1)(b) an application for a restraint order under section 11(1)(b)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b) without notice
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(1) the application is made as the Rule requires` `o 67 r 2(1)(b) an application for a restraint order under section 11(1)(b)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: (b) with notice
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(1) the application is made as the Rule requires` `o 67 r 2(1) another application` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the paragraph speaks only of (a) and (b)
-- r 2(2).  Arguments: owner known; entitled in the matter of the owner naming the defendant; entitled in the matter of the Act; later documents so entitled.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(2) the application is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- all entitled
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(2) the application is entitled as the Rule requires` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the owner is not known: "if known"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(2) the application is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- known owner not named as defendant
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(2) the application is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not entitled in the matter of the Act
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(2) the application is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- later documents not so entitled
-- r 2(3).  Arguments: a warrant application; supported by an affidavit; ground (i); ground (ii); particulars.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(3) the affidavit supports the application for a warrant as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)(i) and (b)
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(3) the affidavit supports the application for a warrant as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)(ii) and (b)
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(3) the affidavit supports the application for a warrant as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- neither ground stated
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(3) the affidavit supports the application for a warrant as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- particulars missing
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(3) the affidavit supports the application for a warrant as the Rule requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: no affidavit
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(3) the affidavit supports the application for a warrant as the Rule requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an application under paragraph (1)(a)
-- r 2(4).  Arguments: a restraint order application; supported by an affidavit; ground (i); ground (ii); situation stated.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(4) the affidavit supports the application for a restraint order as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)(i) and (b)
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(4) the affidavit supports the application for a restraint order as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)(ii) and (b)
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(4) the affidavit supports the application for a restraint order as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- no ground
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(4) the affidavit supports the application for a restraint order as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- (b) not stated
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(4) the affidavit supports the application for a restraint order as the Rule requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: no affidavit
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(4) the affidavit supports the application for a restraint order as the Rule requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an application under paragraph (1)(b)
-- r 2(5).
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(5) the form of the warrant for search and seizure` EQUALS "97" -- "must be in Form 97"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(5) the warrant for search and seizure is in the form the Rule requires` "97" EQUALS JUST TRUE -- Form 97
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(5) the warrant for search and seizure is in the form the Rule requires` "96" EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: another form
-- r 2(6).  Companion: a restraint order is issued.  Then (a): issued; the Court otherwise provides.  Then compliance: (a) applies; served on the defendant; served on others; issued.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(6) the duties of the Public Prosecutor to serve arise` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "Where a restraint order is issued under section 11(1)(b)"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(6) the duties of the Public Prosecutor to serve arise` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the "Where" is not met
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(6)(a) the requirement to serve copies of the order and affidavit on the defendant applies` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- issued and no contrary provision
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(6)(a) the requirement to serve copies of the order and affidavit on the defendant applies` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "unless the Court otherwise provides"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(6)(a) the requirement to serve copies of the order and affidavit on the defendant applies` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no restraint order issued
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(6) the Public Prosecutor has served as the Rule requires` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a) and (b) done
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(6) the Public Prosecutor has served as the Rule requires` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: (a) not done
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(6) the Public Prosecutor has served as the Rule requires` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: (b) not done
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(6) the Public Prosecutor has served as the Rule requires` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the Court provided otherwise, so (a) is not needed and (b) is done
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(6) the Public Prosecutor has served as the Rule requires` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the Court provided otherwise but (b) is not done
#ASSERT `o 67 r 2(6) the Public Prosecutor has served as the Rule requires` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no restraint order issued: QD, the duty does not arise

§ `O 67 r 3`
#ASSERT `o 67 r 3(1) the application is made by summons as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- by summons
#ASSERT `o 67 r 3(1) the application is made by summons as the Rule requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: not by summons
#ASSERT `o 67 r 3(1) the application is made by summons as the Rule requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an application by the Public Prosecutor under section 18
-- r 3(2).  Arguments: an application to revoke or vary; the date by which all were served; the last day.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 3(2) the application and affidavit are filed and served within the period` TRUE (JUST (Date 24 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- served on the last day: within 14 days
#ASSERT `o 67 r 3(2) the application and affidavit are filed and served within the period` TRUE (JUST (Date 20 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- served earlier
#ASSERT `o 67 r 3(2) the application and affidavit are filed and served within the period` TRUE (JUST (Date 25 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- served the day after the last day: "within 14 days"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 3(2) the application and affidavit are filed and served within the period` TRUE NOTHING (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- not yet served on everyone: the period may still be running
#ASSERT `o 67 r 3(2) the application and affidavit are filed and served within the period` FALSE (JUST (Date 20 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- not an application to revoke or vary a warrant or an order under section 11(1)
#ASSERT `o 67 r 3(2) the period for filing and serving`'s `period length` EQUALS 14 -- "within 14 days after the date of filing"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 3(2) the period for filing and serving`'s `period unit` EQUALS Days -- days
#ASSERT `o 67 r 3(2) the period for filing and serving`'s `period direction` EQUALS `After the anchor` -- after

§ `O 67 r 4`
-- Arguments: an application under s 19(1) by an interested person; for an order or permission; the date by which all were filed and served; the last day.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 4 the application and affidavit are filed and served in time` TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 20 3 2025)) (Date 21 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- served before the last day (at least 2 clear days before the hearing)
#ASSERT `o 67 r 4 the application and affidavit are filed and served in time` TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 21 3 2025)) (Date 21 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- served on the last day
#ASSERT `o 67 r 4 the application and affidavit are filed and served in time` TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 22 3 2025)) (Date 21 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- served after the last day: less than 2 clear days
#ASSERT `o 67 r 4 the application and affidavit are filed and served in time` TRUE TRUE NOTHING (Date 21 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- not yet served on everyone
#ASSERT `o 67 r 4 the application and affidavit are filed and served in time` FALSE TRUE (JUST (Date 20 3 2025)) (Date 21 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- not by a person with an interest under section 19(1)
#ASSERT `o 67 r 4 the application and affidavit are filed and served in time` TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 20 3 2025)) (Date 21 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- not for an order under section 19(4) or permission to examine
#ASSERT `o 67 r 4 the period before the hearing`'s `period length` EQUALS 2 -- "at least 2 clear days"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 4 the period before the hearing`'s `period unit` EQUALS `Clear days` -- clear days
#ASSERT `o 67 r 4 the period before the hearing`'s `period direction` EQUALS `Before the anchor` -- before the date fixed for the hearing

§ `O 67 r 5`
-- r 5(1).  Arguments: the Public Prosecutor's application under s 20(3); supported by an affidavit; states the basis.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 5(1) the application is supported by the affidavit the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- supported, stating the basis
#ASSERT `o 67 r 5(1) the application is supported by the affidavit the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: affidavit does not state the basis
#ASSERT `o 67 r 5(1) the application is supported by the affidavit the Rule requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: no affidavit
#ASSERT `o 67 r 5(1) the application is supported by the affidavit the Rule requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an application under section 20(3)
-- r 5(2).
#ASSERT `o 67 r 5(2) the application and affidavit are filed and served within the period` TRUE (JUST (Date 24 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- on the last day
#ASSERT `o 67 r 5(2) the application and affidavit are filed and served within the period` TRUE (JUST (Date 25 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- after the last day
#ASSERT `o 67 r 5(2) the application and affidavit are filed and served within the period` TRUE NOTHING (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- not yet served
#ASSERT `o 67 r 5(2) the application and affidavit are filed and served within the period` FALSE (JUST (Date 20 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- not the paragraph (1) application
#ASSERT `o 67 r 5(2) the period for filing and serving`'s `period length` EQUALS 14 -- "within 14 days after the date of filing"

§ `O 67 r 6`
-- r 6(2).  Arguments: the Public Trustee is appointed under s 15; the requirement.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 6(2) the requirement is necessary` TRUE `o 67 r 6(2) an affidavit of fitness sworn by the Public Trustee` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "It is not necessary for an affidavit of fitness to be sworn"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 6(2) the requirement is necessary` TRUE `o 67 r 6(2) security given by the Public Trustee` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "or for the Public Trustee to give security"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 6(2) the requirement is necessary` TRUE `o 67 r 6 another requirement of Order 13, Rule 9` EQUALS NOTHING -- the paragraph speaks only of those two
#ASSERT `o 67 r 6(2) the requirement is necessary` FALSE `o 67 r 6(2) security given by the Public Trustee` EQUALS NOTHING -- no Public Trustee appointed under section 15
-- r 6(1).
#ASSERT `o 67 r 6(1) the requirement of Order 13, Rule 9 applies` TRUE `o 67 r 6 another requirement of Order 13, Rule 9` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "Order 13, Rule 9 applies where the Public Trustee is appointed under section 15"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 6(1) the requirement of Order 13, Rule 9 applies` TRUE `o 67 r 6(2) security given by the Public Trustee` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "Subject to paragraph (2)"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 6(1) the requirement of Order 13, Rule 9 applies` TRUE `o 67 r 6(2) an affidavit of fitness sworn by the Public Trustee` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "Subject to paragraph (2)"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 6(1) the requirement of Order 13, Rule 9 applies` FALSE `o 67 r 6 another requirement of Order 13, Rule 9` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the "where" is not met

§ `O 67 r 7`
-- r 7(1).  Arguments: an application under s 16(2) by an appointee; filed and served with an affidavit; particulars; reasons.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 7(1) the application is filed and served with the affidavit the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- affidavit with (a) and (b)
#ASSERT `o 67 r 7(1) the application is filed and served with the affidavit the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- (a) missing
#ASSERT `o 67 r 7(1) the application is filed and served with the affidavit the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- (b) missing
#ASSERT `o 67 r 7(1) the application is filed and served with the affidavit the Rule requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: no affidavit
#ASSERT `o 67 r 7(1) the application is filed and served with the affidavit the Rule requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a destruction-order application
-- r 7(2).
#ASSERT `o 67 r 7(2) the application and affidavit are served within the period` TRUE (JUST (Date 24 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- on the last day
#ASSERT `o 67 r 7(2) the application and affidavit are served within the period` TRUE (JUST (Date 25 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- after the last day
#ASSERT `o 67 r 7(2) the application and affidavit are served within the period` TRUE NOTHING (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- not yet served
#ASSERT `o 67 r 7(2) the application and affidavit are served within the period` FALSE (JUST (Date 20 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- not the paragraph (1) application
#ASSERT `o 67 r 7(2) the period for serving`'s `period length` EQUALS 14 -- "within 14 days after the date of filing"

§ `O 67 r 8`
-- r 8(1).  Arguments: a forfeiture application; owner known; entitled naming the defendant; entitled in the matter of the Act; later documents.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(1) the application is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- all entitled
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(1) the application is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- owner not known: "if known"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(1) the application is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- known owner not named
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(1) the application is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not entitled in the matter of the Act
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(1) the application is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- later documents not so entitled
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(1) the application is entitled as the Rule requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an application for forfeiture under section 21
-- r 8(2).  Arguments: a forfeiture application; filed and served with an affidavit; ground (i); ground (ii); particulars; warrant or order stated.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(2) the application is filed and served with the affidavit the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)(i), (b), (c)
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(2) the application is filed and served with the affidavit the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)(ii), (b), (c)
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(2) the application is filed and served with the affidavit the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- no ground
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(2) the application is filed and served with the affidavit the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- (b) missing
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(2) the application is filed and served with the affidavit the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- (c) missing
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(2) the application is filed and served with the affidavit the Rule requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: no affidavit
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(2) the application is filed and served with the affidavit the Rule requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a forfeiture application
-- r 8(3).
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(3) the application and affidavit are served within the period` TRUE (JUST (Date 24 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- on the last day
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(3) the application and affidavit are served within the period` TRUE (JUST (Date 25 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- after the last day
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(3) the application and affidavit are served within the period` TRUE NOTHING (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- not yet served
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(3) the application and affidavit are served within the period` FALSE (JUST (Date 20 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- not the paragraph (1) application
#ASSERT `o 67 r 8(3) the period for serving`'s `period length` EQUALS 14 -- "within 14 days after the date of filing"

§ `O 67 r 9`
-- Arguments: an application under s 27(1); the date by which all were filed and served; the last day.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 9 the application and affidavit are filed and served within the period` TRUE (JUST (Date 24 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- on the last day
#ASSERT `o 67 r 9 the application and affidavit are filed and served within the period` TRUE (JUST (Date 25 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- after the last day
#ASSERT `o 67 r 9 the application and affidavit are filed and served within the period` TRUE NOTHING (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- not yet served
#ASSERT `o 67 r 9 the application and affidavit are filed and served within the period` FALSE (JUST (Date 20 3 2025)) (Date 24 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- not an application under section 27(1)
#ASSERT `o 67 r 9 the period for filing and serving`'s `period length` EQUALS 14 -- "within 14 days after the date of filing"

§ `O 67 r 10`
-- Arguments: the document was filed under this Order; a Judge's permission has been given; the keel's answer on whether the person who gave it is a Judge.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 10 the person may inspect or take a copy of the document` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no permission
#ASSERT `o 67 r 10 the person may inspect or take a copy of the document` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING -- QA: permission of a Judge lifts the bar and grants nothing
#ASSERT `o 67 r 10 the person may inspect or take a copy of the document` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- permission given by someone who is not a Judge
#ASSERT `o 67 r 10 the person may inspect or take a copy of the document` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE -- permission by someone not shown to be a Judge leaves the bar standing
#ASSERT `o 67 r 10 the person may inspect or take a copy of the document` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING -- a document not filed under this Order
#ASSERT `o 67 r 10 inspecting or taking a copy of the document is barred` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- no permission
#ASSERT `o 67 r 10 inspecting or taking a copy of the document is barred` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the Judge's permission lifts the bar
#ASSERT `o 67 r 10 inspecting or taking a copy of the document is barred` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- permission by a non-Judge does not lift it
#ASSERT `o 67 r 10 inspecting or taking a copy of the document is barred` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING -- a document not filed under this Order

§ `O 67 -- the duties as regulative rules`
-- Where the text gives 14 days the rule carries WITHIN 14.  The time unit of the trace is one day.
-- expected: FULFILLED (done on day 10)
#TRACE `o 67 r 3(2) the Public Prosecutor's duty to file and serve` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 67 the Public Prosecutor` DOES `o 67 file and serve the application and affidavit` AT 10
-- expected: BREACH (done on day 15)
#TRACE `o 67 r 3(2) the Public Prosecutor's duty to file and serve` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 67 the Public Prosecutor` DOES `o 67 file and serve the application and affidavit` AT 15
-- expected: FULFILLED (day 14)
#TRACE `o 67 r 7(2) the applicant's duty to serve` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 67 the applicant` DOES `o 67 file and serve the application and affidavit` AT 14
-- expected: BREACH (nothing done by day 20)
#TRACE `o 67 r 7(2) the applicant's duty to serve` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 20)
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `o 67 r 2(6) the Public Prosecutor's duty to serve the restraint order` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 67 the Public Prosecutor` DOES `o 67 serve copies of the restraint order` AT 2
-- expected: BREACH (a person inspected without a Judge's permission)
#TRACE `o 67 r 10 the prohibition on inspecting a document filed under this Order` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 67 any person` DOES `o 67 inspect or take a copy of a document filed under this Order without the permission of a Judge` AT 1

§ `Fix round -- the persons on whom the Rule 4 application must be served`
-- Arguments: the application is under section 19(1) by an interested person; it is for an order under section 19(4) or permission to examine; the person.
#ASSERT `o 67 r 4 the application and affidavit must be served on the person` TRUE TRUE `o 67 r 4(c) the Public Prosecutor` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (c): service on the Public Prosecutor is required
#ASSERT `o 67 r 4 the application and affidavit must be served on the person` TRUE TRUE `o 67 r 4(d) any other person having an interest in the property to which the application relates` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (d)
#ASSERT `o 67 r 4 the application and affidavit must be served on the person` TRUE TRUE `o 67 r 4(e) any person appointed under section 15(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (e)
#ASSERT `o 67 r 4 the application and affidavit must be served on the person` TRUE TRUE `o 67 r 4 another person` EQUALS NOTHING -- a person the Rule does not list: no "only"
#ASSERT `o 67 r 4 the application and affidavit must be served on the person` FALSE TRUE `o 67 r 4(c) the Public Prosecutor` EQUALS NOTHING -- not an application of the kind Rule 4 names
#ASSERT `o 67 r 4 the application and affidavit must be served on the person` TRUE FALSE `o 67 r 4(c) the Public Prosecutor` EQUALS NOTHING -- not for an order under section 19(4) or permission to examine

